From f2b787f3c15001811f0e918f8c559a52e8d1a772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:41:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/36] B70-QSA-K01: attn2 sparse GQA path for Xe2
 (B70_QSA_ATTN_IMPL=attn2), no register spills

The splitk kernel holds a [BLOCK_M, HEAD_DIM] fp32 accumulator plus gathered
K/V tiles per program; at head_dim 256 every BMG config spills 11-46 KB per
thread, and extra warps only replicate work (Intel lays a chained dot's warps
on M = 8 heads). attn2 follows the SYCL kernels' shape inside Triton: one
subgroup per (row, KV group, tile of BLOCK_N selected tokens); Q.K and P.V
run head_dim chunk by chunk in runtime loops with each output chunk stored
at once; each tile writes an fp32 partial (normalised output + log2-sum-exp);
an online LSE merge applies BF16 rounding and the sigmoid gate. Rows go in
chunks to bound the partial workspace.

Default stays splitk. Defaults compile with zero spill on BMG-G31 (Triton
3.8.0+xpu, IGC 2.41.5, AOT): decode BLOCK_N 32 x 4 chunks, prefill
BLOCK_N 64 x 8 chunks. Tune keys sparse_attn2_decode/_prefill. Warmup
compiles the attn2 profiles when the env selects it. Untimed on GPU.
